<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lysander</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 395 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lysander was a Spartan admiral and statesman who won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-war">Peloponnesian War</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a>. With Persian money from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-younger">Cyrus the Younger</a> he built a fleet that destroyed the Athenian navy at Aegospotami in 405 BCE, then blockaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> into surrender in 404 BCE. He installed pro-Spartan oligarchies across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> and was killed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haliartus">Haliartus</a> in 395 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lysander.jpg" alt="Lysander" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 19th century lithograph, unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lysander_outside_the_walls_of_Athens_19th_century_lithograph.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
